First context restoration observation, 2026-10-08, same canvas2d-678 browser session:
- A separate WebGL2 canvas was created but not attached to the document.
- WEBGL_lose_context loss event was awaited, then restoreContext() was called.
- Chromium console: `WebGL: INVALID_OPERATION: restoreContext: context restoration not allowed`.
- The awaited restore event did not arrive; the CLI evaluation was interrupted (exit 130).
- This was not counted as a passing lifecycle observation.

Affected-flow repair:
- Repeated the context-loss/restore/dispose observation on a separate canvas attached to document.body.
- The loss and restore events both arrived. Render while lost returned CONTEXT_LOST.
- After restore the context reported 8 stencil bits. Program, buffer and VAO existed before dispose and were invalid after dispose.

UI tool repair:
- After a reload, Reset v2 reference e4 was stale. A fresh snapshot returned f1e4; clicking it passed.
